    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/3/83108.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, I mean, one big thing that I hear a lot from my constituents is folks are very concerned about how we're educating our children. And it can feel hopeless if you look to Washington to solve that problem. The truth is a local school board. You have a local superintendent. And that's who's going to make those decisions anyway. You really can move the needle in those conversations if you're organized and you're aggressive and you go out and you have those conversations. I think that's the best way to influence all",
