    "turn_idx": 55,
    "turn_text": "So far, I've been reasonably pleased with President Biden's rhetoric on China. Admittedly, I was very concerned as his previous dealings with China were not what I would have wanted. And frankly, I had to pass a bill to reverse something that he put in when he was Vice President. But so far, I've been cautiously optimistic on the tone and the tenor there. Obviously, you know, my role is to make part of my role is to make sure that that relationship moves in the direction that I think is best from a national security and economic security standpoint. So we'll continue to provide that oversight. But I have been reasonably pleased so far and I have always found good colleagues on the other side of the aisle to work with on the China issue.",
