    "turn_text": "Well, another one of your house that you sit on is the climate crisis. And we talked about something on political playlists that you mentioned from, you know, being put on this committee was The world is moving and correct me if I'm wrong, but the world is moving towards renewable energy. And what we should start figuring out is how do we manufacture those technologies in the United States? And it was the first time I really heard a politician say that. And I really resonated with me because I work in the solar industry. And when we try and get panels, 90% of the world panels are made in China. And it always sort of boggled my mind that this was something that we couldn't be doing here. So I'd love to hear your thoughts on it and your goals for this committee as well.",
