    "turn_idx": 66,
    "turn_text": "Well, we're slow. You know, we are. You know, my personal view is the rhetoric outpaced the reality, you know, and you had people saying crazy things like if we didn't go completely net zero in 10 years, the world was going to end. I mean, it's just not helpful, frankly, because it's not realistic. That's not going to happen. And so I think the rhetoric outpaced the reality and now that people are taking a sober look at where we are from a technology standpoint, from a deployment standpoint. I think the rubber is starting to meet the road a little bit and we're getting hopefully some more sober policy ideas in place. And again, for me, it's all about innovation. I think we have to do",
